        guideHtml: `
            <p class="bg-orange-50 border border-orange-200 p-3.5 rounded-xl text-zinc-800"><strong>Basic rule:</strong> Write one command per line. First the name (e.g. <code>A =</code>) and then the command with values inside parentheses <code>( )</code>.</p>
            <div class="bg-white border border-stone-200 rounded-xl p-3.5"><div class="font-display font-bold text-zinc-900 text-base">1. Draw a point</div><code class="block bg-zinc-900 text-amber-200 p-2.5 rounded-lg my-2 font-semibold">A = point(3, 2)</code><p class="text-stone-600">Places point <strong>A</strong> by moving <strong>3</strong> units right (x) and <strong>2</strong> units up (y).</p></div>
            <div class="bg-white border border-stone-200 rounded-xl p-3.5"><div class="font-display font-bold text-zinc-900 text-base">2. Connect two points (segment)</div><code class="block bg-zinc-900 text-amber-200 p-2.5 rounded-lg my-2 font-semibold">s1 = line(A, B)</code><p class="text-stone-600">Draws a straight line from <strong>A</strong> to <strong>B</strong>. You can also write <code>line(0, 0, 3, 2)</code> or <code>line(A, B, 5)</code> for length 5.</p></div>
            <div class="bg-white border border-stone-200 rounded-xl p-3.5"><div class="font-display font-bold text-zinc-900 text-base">3. Draw an arc or circle</div><code class="block bg-zinc-900 text-amber-200 p-2.5 rounded-lg my-2 font-semibold">arco1 = arc(A, 4, 0, 90)<br>c1 = arc(A, 4, 0, 360)</code><p class="text-stone-600">Use <code>arc(center, radius, start, sweep)</code>. With <strong>360</strong> degrees you draw a full circle. Or use <code>arc(A, B, A, 0, 360)</code> to open the compass from A to B.</p></div>
            <div class="bg-white border border-stone-200 rounded-xl p-3.5"><div class="font-display font-bold text-zinc-900 text-base">4. Midpoint (interpolate)</div><code class="block bg-zinc-900 text-amber-200 p-2.5 rounded-lg my-2 font-semibold">M = point(interpolate(A, B, 0.5))</code><p class="text-stone-600">Finds point <strong>M</strong> halfway between A and B (with <strong>0.5</strong>). Always wrap it inside <code>point(...)</code> to draw it.</p></div>
            <div class="bg-white border border-stone-200 rounded-xl p-3.5"><div class="font-display font-bold text-zinc-900 text-base">5. Perpendicular line (90°)</div><code class="block bg-zinc-900 text-amber-200 p-2.5 rounded-lg my-2 font-semibold">perp(s1, P)</code><p class="text-stone-600">Draws a 90° line relative to <strong>s1</strong> passing through <strong>P</strong> (optional length: <code>perp(s1, P, 6)</code>).</p></div>
            <div class="bg-white border border-stone-200 rounded-xl p-3.5"><div class="font-display font-bold text-zinc-900 text-base">6. Parallel line</div><code class="block bg-zinc-900 text-amber-200 p-2.5 rounded-lg my-2 font-semibold">parallel(s1, P)</code><p class="text-stone-600">Draws a line parallel to <strong>s1</strong> passing through <strong>P</strong> (or <code>parallel(s1, P, 6)</code>).</p></div>
            <div class="bg-white border border-stone-200 rounded-xl p-3.5"><div class="font-display font-bold text-zinc-900 text-base">7. Intersection point</div><code class="block bg-zinc-900 text-amber-200 p-2.5 rounded-lg my-2 font-semibold">C = point(intersect(c1, c2, 1))</code><p class="text-stone-600">Finds point <strong>C</strong> where <strong>c1</strong> and <strong>c2</strong> cross (<code>1</code> for first crossing, <code>2</code> for second). Always wrap in <code>point(...)</code>.</p></div>
            <div class="bg-white border border-stone-200 rounded-xl p-3.5"><div class="font-display font-bold text-zinc-900 text-base">8. Stroke, fill & colors (Settings)</div><code class="block bg-zinc-900 text-amber-200 p-2.5 rounded-lg my-2 font-semibold">stroke(s1, 5)<br>fill(c1, 0.4)</code><p class="text-stone-600">Use <code>stroke(object, number)</code> to change <strong>line thickness</strong>, and <code>fill(object, 0.4)</code> to fill shapes. Tap the colored dot next to each line number in the editor (or <strong>Settings</strong>) to choose a <strong>color</strong>.</p></div>
        `
